// The repository holds two modules: go-tony, the library and the o command, and
// git-issue, the tracker, which imports go-tony by version. This joins them for
// local work, so git-issue builds against the go-tony in this checkout rather
// than the last release, and gopls sees both. go install ...@latest ignores it,
// as it should: a release of git-issue pins the go-tony it was built with.
go 1.27.1

use (
	./git-issue
	./go-tony
)
